# SkySpy vLLM — best config from the DGX Spark tuning runs (2026-07-24).
# WINNER (Bayesian-tuned, blended reward 0.6 quality / 0.4 speed):
#   Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507-FP8  reward=0.8198  quality=0.719 (pass 0.75)  speed=0.97
#
# The tuner took the station's own MoE model and made it BOTH higher quality and
# fast: max_model_len=8192 flips the assistant into COMPACT MODE (short system
# prompt + terse tool descriptions), which this model handles far better than the
# full 32k prompt (quality 0.56 -> 0.75); fp8 KV cache keeps decode near the top
# speed. Beats the untuned baseline (0.59) and the dense 32B-AWQ (0.665) from the
# first run.
#
# Ranked (final study): 30B-A3B@8192/fp8 0.820 > 7B 0.629 > 30B-A3B@32768 0.592 > 30B-A3B@16384 0.476
# Also tested: gpt-oss-20b serves fine but scored quality 0.0 — its harmony
# tool-calling doesn't work through SkySpy's LangChain agent (needs adapter work).
#
# Apply: drop into .env, then `docker compose --profile gpu up -d vllm`.
VLLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507-FP8
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS=32
VLLM_MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=4096
VLLM_KV_CACHE_DTYPE=fp8
VLLM_TOOL_PARSER=hermes
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--no-enable-prefix-caching --enable-chunked-prefill
# DGX Spark (GB10) launch requirements, baked into tuning/vllm/ defaults:
#   VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM=0  (DeepGemm FP8 MoE kernel asserts on Blackwell)
#   gpu-util <= 0.85      (128 GB is unified with the system)
# Prod sip-ai-vllm already runs this model — it only needs the tuned knobs above.
